{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ropes\/rope"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Ropes\/documentation\/Ropes"]]},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"symbol","title":"Rope","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Rope"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"Ropes"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Rope","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:5Ropes4RopeV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Ropes\/Rope.swift#L26","fileName":"Rope.swift"},"roleHeading":"Structure"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A rope: a sequence stored as a balanced tree of chunks, so inserting, removing or replacing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements anywhere costs O(log "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") plus the elements moved within one chunk, rather than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":") an array spends shifting everything after the edit."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Rope","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The chunks, each up to a few kilobytes of elements, are the vertices of an AVL tree in flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrays, in sequence order, and each vertex records how many elements its subtree holds, so an"},{"type":"text","tex